  "sourceGuidance": [
   {
    "title": "ORT Scoring & Interpretation",
    "text": "Scores range from 0 to 26. The scores are categorized into three risk categories.\n– Low Risk= Scores 0-3 – Moderate Risk = scores 4 – 7 – High risk = Scores 8 or more\nAccording to the validation sample (Webster, 2005) patients in the low risk category have a 5.6% chance of developing one or more aberrant behaviour when prescribed opioids. The moderate risk category had a risk of 28% while the high risk category had a risk of 91%. Note that these percentages are not direct measures of risk of opioid abuse or dependence, but rather aberrant behaviours (which are known to be associated with abuse and dependence). Aberrant behaviours are defined as:\n-Used additional opioids than those prescribed -Used additional opioids than those prescribed more than once -Forged prescription -Sold prescription -Admitted to seeking euphoria from opioids -Admitted to wanting opioids for anxiety -Overdose and death -Injected drug -Abnormal urine/blood screen -Abnormal urine/blood screen positive for 2 or more substances -Solicited opioids from other providers -Unauthorized ER visits -Concurrent abuse of alcohol -Unauthorized dose escalation\n",
    "source_url": null
   }
  ],
